// LAINFLAGS: --engine=ir-full
// The element range survives a SUBSLICE. `var s = xs[1..4]` stores an address, which marks the
// array escaped, and the slice is round-tripped through a slot, which launders provenance —
// so the whole subslice family lost the range for two independent reasons. Both are handled:
//
//   · an escape only forfeits the range when something can EXERCISE it. A callee is the only
//     thing that writes through an escaped address with no IR_STORE here to see, so with no
//     call in the function the stores are the complete set of writers.
//   · a LOAD from a slot written EXACTLY ONCE is that stored value, so provenance survives it.
//
// The second subslice below makes the chain eight hops (make_slice, elem_ptr, slice_data and a
// load-through-slot per level), which is why the walk allows twenty-four.
//
// element_range_subslice_fail.ln is the direction that matters: a callee that rewrites the
// array through the slice makes the join stale, and must keep failing.
proc main() i32 {
    var xs i32[5] = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]
    var s = xs[1..4]
    var t = s[1..3]
    return s[0] + t[0] - 50
}
